{
  "dom_id": "step-q92829",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Liam wants to paint a fence. He knows he needs $2$ liters of paint for $32$ square meters of fence. He creates a ratio table to determine the ratio of the volume of paint to the fenced area for different quantities.\n\n| Fence area (square meters) | Paint (liters) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $32$ | $2$ |\n| $80$ | $?$ |\n| $160$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat volume of paint does Liam need to paint $80$ square meters of the fence?",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $32:2$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{32}{2}\n$$\n\nNow we divide the numerator and the denominator by $2$ to find an equivalent ratio:\n\n$$\n\\frac{32÷2}{2÷2}=\\frac{16}{1}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the area of the fence in ${\\text{m}}^{2}$ ($16$), and the denominator represents the volume of paint in liters ($1$).\n\nWe can make a numerator of $80$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\times 5}{1\\times 5} & =\\frac{80}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| Fence area (square meters) | Paint (liters) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $32$ | $2$ |\n| $80$ | $5$ |\n| $160$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, Liam needs $5$ liters of paint for $80$ square meters of the fence.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
